- helm
- pass
- scope
- scope_foot
- scope_mount
- weave

' The host pack's own foot. A world that keeps places for others and is a
' tenant of a host asks that host to run the world prepared for each
' place: for every place of a scope this world keeps that holds a minted
' name and no world yet, one record beneath this world's seat as a tenant
' (extras/mounts/host: worlds/[w]) that names the world and the founding
' it starts under, and says it is to run. So a world an invitation was
' minted for is already running, on the inviter's host, when the
' invitation is taken.
'
' Nothing says where a world asks but the compositions themselves: it
' asks wherever it fills a tenant's seat, in whichever composition it
' takes part in that was made from this pack. A machine's own world, which
' keeps the host and fills a tenant's seat in it, asks itself; a world a
' host started for a tenant's seat asks that host for the worlds of what
' it keeps in turn. A world that is no tenant asks nobody. A composition
' whose own record says elsewhere is passed over: the worlds of its
' places are started by someone else (a fleet's machines are). What a world
' starts with is the host's to say, so an ask leaves it out. Nothing here
' starts anything: whoever supervises the machine reads the asks (x/host).
+ host_mount
  + home
    \ self=iota
    ^ path
    [self 'io 'host]
  + stencil
    ' The row of this pack's table where a tenant asks, as a world that
    ' holds the pack names it.
    ^ str
    "/gov/host/worlds"
  + seats
    ' Where this world asks for worlds: beneath each tenant's seat it
    ' fills, on its own side of the composition that seat is in.
    \ state=namespace
    ^ row[path]
    = none=row[path] []
      free=row[weave/bind] []
      tail=path ['worlds]
    | (scope_foot/parts state).fold none
      \ acc=row[path] found=[c=weave/comp s=weave/side]
      ^ row[path]
      = [c s] found
      | c.table.fold acc
        \ out=row[path] p=weave/position
        ^ row[path]
        ? !(equal[str] p.stencil host_mount/stencil) out
        ?> (./some seat) (weave/seat_of c s p.writer.seats free s.me state) out
        = under=path s.root.weld(seat).weld(tail)
        | out.snoc(under)
  + spelled
    ' A world's name as it is written: 0x and its digits.
    \ name=nat
    ^ str
    = at=path [($x name)]
      text (path_show at)
    | text.slice(1 text.len)
  + ask
    \ name=nat made=pass/founding first=myth mounts=str
    ^ myth
    . (myth/sing ['name] (pails/t (host_mount/spelled name)))
      put(['founding] (pails/t (pass/birth made (pass/sent (pass/of first)))))
      put(['mounts] (pails/t mounts))
      put(['run] (pails/n 1))
  + wanted
    ' The asks one scope's places call for, beneath a base, that are not
    ' there yet.
    \ root=path base=path mounts=str acc=row[[p=path q=writ]] state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    | (sovereign_peek root state).tap.fold acc
      \ out [place seat]
      = name seat.nat_at(['name] 0)
        card=path [state.self 'io 'mesa ($x name)]
      ? (eq 0 seat.nat_at(['invite] 0)) out
      ? (eq 0 name) out
      ? (gt seat.nat_at(['world] 0) 0) out
      ?> (./some made) (pass/founded card state) out
      ?> (./some first) (pass/kept (pass/at card 1) state) out
      ?> (./some tail) (path_parse (str/cat_all ["/n" (nat/show name)])) out
      = target=path base.weld(tail)
      ? (maybe/is_some (sovereign_care .x target state).fil) out
      | out.snoc([target (writ/make (host_mount/ask name made first mounts))])
  + asks
    ' Every ask this world owes its host, as it stands: one for each
    ' invited place of every scope it keeps, beneath the first tenant's
    ' seat it fills.
    \ state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      self state.self
      nothing=str ""
      bases (host_mount/seats state)
    ? (eq 0 bases.len) none
    = base bases.at(0)
    | (sovereign_peek (scope_foot/home self) state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel kept]
      ? !(eq rel.len 1) acc
      ?> (./some root) (scope_foot/rooted kept) acc
      ? (gt (sovereign_care .x root state).fil.fall(myth/new).nat_at(['elsewhere] 0) 0) acc
      | host_mount/wanted root base nothing acc state
  + start
    \ server=nat self=iota arguments=row[str]
    ^ nat
    | scope_mount/hand server (host_mount/home self) host_mount/asks
